WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:04.780
Check out these two Saudi princes.

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:08.300
This one's the 57 year old crown prince,

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.560
And this one (the one doing all the hand kissing)
is his younger cousin.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:17.180
Listen to what the older cousin is saying:

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:30.740
He’s being forced to
give up his power and to pass the crown prince title

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:34.060
to his younger cousin, a guy who's almost half his age.

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:36.880
This is Mohammed bin Salman.

00:00:37.540 --> 00:00:39.660
In the West we just call him MBS.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:45.840
And since this moment in June he’s
consolidated power so swiftly and so thoroughly

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.160
that in Saudi Arabia they just know him as

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:53.840
As crown prince, MBS will become king

00:00:54.020 --> 00:00:59.080
And with all of this new power,  MBS is seeking to assert
his dominance throughout the Middle East

00:00:59.300 --> 00:01:04.600
One of his big policies has been a vehement opposition to Saudi Arabia's neighbor, Iran.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:08.220
On that note he's found an ally in the White House.

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:13.540
Inside the kingdom, MBS is also seeking to
cement his authority

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:15.360
and his dominance over the Royal Family.

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:19.940
Saudi Arabia's young crown prince arresting hundreds of his own cousins

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.480
Crackdown on corruption

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.620
11 princes and nearly 40 current or former officials detained,

00:01:25.620 --> 00:01:28.700
reportedly being held at the lavish Ritz Carlton.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:32.460
(Yes, if you’re a Saudi Prince, "jail"
is the Ritz Carlton.)

00:01:32.469 --> 00:01:38.649
MBS called this a corruption crackdown and he branded
himself as the financially responsible anti

00:01:38.649 --> 00:01:39.640
corruption leader.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:43.579
But we’re talking about a guy who recently
purchased one of the most expensive homes

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:48.229
in the world and who last year spent half a billion
dollars on a painting.

00:01:48.229 --> 00:01:52.729
He clearly had other motives for this crackdown beyond fiscal responsibility.

00:01:52.729 --> 00:01:56.359
One thing to realize is that the Saudi royal
family is made up of thousands of members

00:01:56.359 --> 00:02:02.159
who use public money generated from oil revenues
to fund their unthinkably excessive lifestyles.

00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.840
So it wouldn’t be hard for MBS

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.620
to crack down on anyone he wants to.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.960
Coming into power, MBS' second big move

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.960
was to loosen the
strict moral and social rules of the kingdom.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.439
He stripped the religious police of their
right to make arrests.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.660
He expanded women’s right in society including
giving them the right to drive.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:27.740
On the surface, these are progressive social
reforms meant to modernize Saudi society.

00:02:27.740 --> 00:02:32.209
But like the anti corruption crackdowns, the
move is another effort to seize power.

00:02:32.209 --> 00:02:33.959
Saudi society is built on a

00:02:33.959 --> 00:02:39.769
sort of pact between the royal family – just called the
house of Saud – and a vast religious establishment,

00:02:39.769 --> 00:02:42.780
run by conservative Islamic clerics.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:48.689
The clerics give the Saud family legitimacy, by giving them their blessing
as rulers of the kingdom.

00:02:48.689 --> 00:02:53.799
In exchange, the family allows the clerics to
strictly enforce their uncompromising, puritanical

00:02:53.799 --> 00:02:55.969
version of Islam within the kingdom.

00:02:55.969 --> 00:02:59.960
This Faustian bargain means that Saudi princes,
like MBS and others,

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:04.060
can live these indulgent lifestyles and make deals with the West,

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.810
but still retain religious legitimacy in the eyes
of the public.

00:03:06.810 --> 00:03:11.140
It’s a balance that has kept the
Kingdom stable in this very volatile region.

00:03:11.140 --> 00:03:16.079
But now, MBS has violated his family’s part
of the bargain, arresting hard line clerics

00:03:16.080 --> 00:03:18.640
who might speak out against his progressive
reforms.

00:03:18.640 --> 00:03:21.600
This could shake one of the foundational pillars of Saudi society.

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:27.739
The third way MBS is shaking up the kingdom
is his plans for the economy.

00:03:27.739 --> 00:03:30.609
The kingdom’s revenue comes almost entirely
from oil.

00:03:30.609 --> 00:03:36.189
Demand for oil has remained solid for
decades and Saudi Arabia reaped the rewards of that.

00:03:36.189 --> 00:03:39.620
But in 2014, the price of oil started to drop.

00:03:39.620 --> 00:03:44.320
And it became clear that betting the entire kingdom’s
economy on this one resource,

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:46.620
was a dangerous strategy for the future.

00:03:46.620 --> 00:03:51.420
So MBS wants to end what he calls this
“Oil Addiction,” in order to prepare for

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:52.840
a world after oil.

00:03:52.840 --> 00:03:56.700
He’s laid out a vision of privatizing a lot of sectors within the Saudi economy.

00:03:57.380 --> 00:04:00.680
And breaking up this giant, government-owned oil business.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:04.060
But this reform could also create more instability.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:09.400
Thanks to the endless oil money, Saudi citizens
are entitled to a lifelong set of benefits,

00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.900
like free healthcare and subsidized housing.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:14.760
But as MBS tries to privatize the economy

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:15.800
and move away from oil,

00:04:16.060 --> 00:04:19.459
this subsidized lifestyle that so many Saudis enjoy

00:04:19.459 --> 00:04:25.000
could be threatened and the public support that has kept this monarchy so solid for so many years

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:26.530
could begin to dwindle.

00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:31.620
The kingdom of Saudi Arabia is on the brink
of one of the biggest transformations in its history.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:34.460
As this young leader consolidates power

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:37.660
to upend the status quo, he may also upend the

00:04:37.669 --> 00:04:41.740
pillars that have kept the kingdom one
of the more stable countries in the Middle East.

